            "abstract": "<p>\n                    A bijection is proved between\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper S l left-parenthesis n comma bold upper Z right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>Sl</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ⁡\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>,</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mi mathvariant=\"bold\">Z</mml:mi>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname {Sl} (n,{\\mathbf {Z}})</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    -conjugacy classes of hyperbolic matrices with eigenvalues\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartSet lamda 1 comma ellipsis comma lamda Subscript n Baseline EndSet\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:msub>\n                                <mml:mi>\n                                  λ\n                                  \n                                </mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mn>1</mml:mn>\n                              </mml:msub>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo>,</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              …\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>,</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:msub>\n                                <mml:mi>\n                                  λ\n                                  \n                                </mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                              </mml:msub>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\{ {\\lambda _1}, \\ldots ,{\\lambda _n}\\}</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    which are units in an\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"n\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    -degree number field, and narrow ideal classes of the ring\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper R Subscript k Baseline equals bold upper Z left-bracket lamda Subscript i Baseline right-bracket\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:msub>\n                                <mml:mi>R</mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mi>k</mml:mi>\n                              </mml:msub>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo>=</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mi mathvariant=\"bold\">Z</mml:mi>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:msub>\n                                <mml:mi>\n                                  λ\n                                  \n                                </mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mi>i</mml:mi>\n                              </mml:msub>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{R_k} = {\\mathbf {Z}}[{\\lambda _i}]</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    . A bijection between\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper G l left-parenthesis n comma bold upper Z right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>Gl</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ⁡\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>,</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mi mathvariant=\"bold\">Z</mml:mi>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname {Gl} (n,{\\mathbf {Z}})</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    -conjugacy classes and the wide ideal classes, which had been known, is repeated with a different proof.\n                  </p>",
